== emoji sequences: widths against Unicode's table =============
ok   the table has every fully-qualified sequence of Unicode 15.1
ok   each is one cell of two columns, one cluster, written whole 
ok   the standard library alone measures 45 of them as one column
ok   python-wcwidth, the second opinion, agrees with it on those 45
ok   all 45 are an emoji modifier after a base that is text-presentation by default
ok   a skin tone after a raised hand: two columns
ok   text width agrees
ok   a skin tone after a base with emoji presentation: two
ok   a lone variation selector draws nothing
ok   nor does a lone text selector
ok   text width agrees on both
ok   a keycap without the selector (not fully qualified) is one column
ok   a flag is two
ok   a regional indicator alone is one (East Asian Width: neutral; terminals differ)
ok   a combining accent is no column of its own
ok   a ZWJ family is two
ok   wrapping does not split a skin tone off its hand

